## Context
Static audit of tickets/tools/go revealed six concrete smells: redundant disk
re-reads after ensure calls (init.go:93,101,114), hand-rolled JSON via string
concatenation instead of encoding/json (ready.go:153-206), CRLF normalization
duplicated 4× (init.go:230,250,279,307), manual bool-to-string (ready.go:164-172),
silently swallowed EvalSymlinks error (selfupdate.go:66), and a 190-line god
function (ready.go:55-244).

## Actions
1. init.go: replace hasLine/hasManagedBlock re-reads with direct true assignment
2. init.go: extract splitLines helper, replace 4 duplicated CRLF-normalize patterns
3. ready.go: replace hand-rolled JSON with encoding/json marshalling
4. ready.go: extract printReadyJSON and printReadyText helpers from cmdReady
5. selfupdate.go: log EvalSymlinks error instead of silencing with _

## Test
Run `make test` — all existing tests must pass. The JSON output of
`erg ready --json` must be valid JSON (pipe through `jq .` to verify).

## Exit criteria
- All six smells addressed
- `go vet ./...` passes
- `make test` green
- `erg ready --json` output parses as valid JSON
